{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"enchanting-phantastic-weevil","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered by the Step 7 parity sweep while fixing `fernlike-toothsome-hen` (79b2-6ebc-6c1d-4125),\nwhere the MCP edge emitted `307` with a plaintext `http://` Location on the documented client URL.\n\nThe **rule** that bug established: *an https request to this edge must never receive a `Location`\nheader that downgrades the scheme to `http`.* That rule is now enforced for the MCP paths only.\nThe other proxied surfaces on the same port-443 server have no equivalent guarantee.\n\n## Channel census (`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`)\n\n| surface | Location-scheme guarantee |\n|---|---|\n| `location = /mcp/`, `= /mcp`, prefix `/mcp` | ENFORCED by 79b2 (`proxy_redirect` http->https) |\n| `location /review/` (`:92`) | **MISSING** |\n| `location /opcert/` (`:107`) | **MISSING** |\n| `location /` -> Gerrit (`:152`) | **MISSING** |\n| port-80 server | N/A — correctly `301`s to https |\n\nHSTS is NOT part of this gap: 79b2 adds `add_header Strict-Transport-Security ... always;` at the\n443 **server** level, so every surface above already inherits that backstop.\n\n## Why it was left out of 79b2's scope\n\nThe obvious fix — hoisting `proxy_redirect` to the server level — is NOT safe as a drop-in.\n`proxy_redirect` defaults to `default`, which derives its rewrite from **that location's own**\n`proxy_pass`. `/review/` uses `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}/;` (a\nprefix-stripping form), so its `default` rule rewrites the upstream's `http://127.0.0.1:PORT/`\nLocation back to `/review/`. Declaring explicit server-level rules would REPLACE that default and\ncould break the review-bot's relative redirects. Gerrit's block additionally carries a standing\n\"do not add a rewrite here\" constraint for `%2F`-safe proxying (`:145-151`) — `proxy_redirect`\nonly touches response headers, never the request URI, so it is very likely safe there, but that\nneeds to be established rather than assumed.\n\nSo the correct fix is per-surface and needs its own verification, which is more than 79b2's\nblast radius should carry.\n\n## Severity\n\nLower than 79b2. No plaintext Location has been OBSERVED from these three surfaces; this is a\nmissing structural guarantee, not a reproduced downgrade. The 79b2 root cause B\n(`FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` unset, so uvicorn distrusts the forwarded proto) applies specifically to\nthe containerised MCP service; `/review/` and `/opcert/` should be checked for the same posture\nrather than presumed affected or unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] For each of `/review/`, `/opcert/` and Gerrit's `location /`, it is established and\n      recorded whether that upstream can emit an absolute `http://` Location — by inspecting how\n      each app builds redirects and whether it sits behind a proxy-headers trust boundary.\n- [ ] Every surface that CAN emit one carries a `proxy_redirect` rule upgrading it to `https`,\n      added per-location so no existing `default` rule is replaced. Verified by a structural test\n      over `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` that fails if a surface regresses.\n- [ ] `/review/`'s existing `default` proxy_redirect behaviour is preserved — evidenced by\n      showing the prefix-stripping rewrite still applies after the change.\n- [ ] Gerrit's `%2F`-safe proxying is unaffected, evidenced by reasoning or a probe that\n      `proxy_redirect` alters only response headers and not the request URI.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION: an unauthenticated probe of each surface on the deployed edge shows no\n      `http://` Location, recorded in a comment with the actual response headers.\n\n## Notes\n\nReported from unauthenticated probes and repo inspection only. No credential was transmitted.","id":"a61d-adf9-3725-4847","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["nginx","edge","security","parity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"nginx edge has no Location-scheme guarantee for /review/, /opcert/ and Gerrit"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787862229807250462,"uuid":"62c72a5f-e5ce-4b93-b361-5bb7eee79bad"}